      "side": 1,
      "message": "You are right and I was forced to deal with that in the tests already (previous change in the stack). I personally think it makes no sense to check whether user is allowed to do something before we can actually figure out what is that that the user wants (typically in Keystone it is clear, but in case of things like actions this is not the case). But the most weird stuff is feeding of filters into the policy evaluation before we actually even know whether the data passed is valid.\n\nSo yes, we have a behavior change. I can\u0027t imagine we can leak data by telling the user his input was not valid",
